                <pb facs="0551" n="449" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg449"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2261g: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-11T10:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 11, 1919,
                                10 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The Department is replying in the following sense to a note from the French
                    Government dated June 6. You may hand a copy informally to the Minister of
                    Foreign Affairs and request copy of the French note to which reply is made. The
                    Department trusts the Japanese Foreign Office will concur in the position taken
                    by this Government and use its best efforts to make possible an organization
                    meeting in Paris by June 18. Questions of interpretation can be discussed at any
                    time after that.</p>
                <p>[Here follows the text of the reply to the French Government as embodied in the
                    telegram of June 11 to the Ambassador in France, printed <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >supra.</hi>]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
